Modifications to vendored files:

  - renderers/shared/brand-theme.mjs (new file, original work under
      MIT): reads a diagrams-plugin theme.css and returns the style
      block described below.
  - renderers/shared/cli.mjs: imports brand-theme.mjs and injects its
      style block before </head> when ARCHIFY_THEME is set.
  - bin/archify.mjs: accepts a global --theme <path> flag and exports it
      to the renderers as ARCHIFY_THEME.
  - assets/template.html: adds --region-fill and --font-diagram tokens
      to the classic palette; body text, exported SVG text, and region
      fills read those tokens instead of literals; the classic light
      --arrow changes from #94a3b8 to #64748b (2.45:1 to 4.55:1 against
      the light background).
  - brand-marks/catalog.json and renderers/shared/generated-brand-marks.mjs:
      the vue, jenkins, and rust marks are removed because their
      recorded licenses are non-commercial (CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0) or
      share-alike (CC-BY-SA-3.0, CC-BY-SA-4.0). THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
      records the removal.
  - package.json: trimmed to name, version, type, license, bin, and
      engines; development scripts and devDependencies removed.
  - Em-dash (U+2014) and en-dash (U+2013) substitution across every
      vendored text file, per the rules below.

Not vendored: the upstream SKILL.md (this plugin's SKILL.md is
original, adapted from its workflow), the update notifier
(scripts/check-update.mjs, skill-release.json), development generators
(scripts/generate-*.mjs, scripts/update-contract.mjs), the test suite,
package-lock.json, and the pre-rendered example HTML files (the engine's
`examples` command regenerates them).

Em-dash and en-dash substitution rules applied at port time:

  - <space>U+2014<space> as a sentence pause in prose or comments
    becomes ", " (comma + space)
  - <label><space>U+2014<space><description> in labelled bullets,
    headings, and comment banners becomes ": " (colon + space)
  - <digit>U+2013<digit> in numeric ranges becomes "-" (hyphen)
  - U+2014 or U+2013 inside a JavaScript string, template literal,
    regular expression, or JSON string becomes the escape \u2014 or
    \u2013, so runtime output (diagnostic messages, viewer labels)
    stays byte-identical

Verification at port time: the upstream test suite (1398 tests) ran
against the modified engine. Every render, geometry, validation,
routing, and export test passed. The failures were limited to tests
asserting the exact upstream comment wording, checked-in artifacts
rendered from the unmodified template, the exact upstream brand-mark
license inventory, and two release-staging tests that also fail on the
unmodified upstream in this environment.

Adapted from upstream 2 and upstream 1 without vendoring (original text
